# pyright, installed here by `scripts/test-deps.sh pyright` (`npm ci` against
# the package.json and package-lock.json beside this file, which pin it) - the
# language server this plugin's semantic tier (GM-299) drives, and a test
# dependency of this crate the same way rust-analyzer is one of plugins/rust's.
# Only node_modules/ is ignored, exactly as in plugins/typescript: the
# manifest and the lock are committed so the version is recorded (GM-419), the
# installed 34 MB of someone else's package is not.
#
# It lives here rather than inside `conformance/project/` on purpose. The
# conformance kit runs a plugin against a scratch *copy* of the fixture and
# `copy_tree` skips symlinks, so an npm `.bin` directory would not survive the
# copy - and a pyright install inside the fixture would also put 5,205
# bundled typeshed stubs where the walk can see them.
node_modules/
